# {{TEAM_NAME}} — Claude Code (minimal install)

This is a minimal install: the security pipeline is active, memory is a flat
file you can read and edit directly, and nothing else is configured yet. No
persona, no fixed workflow, no required process. Just talk to it.

## Security

Every Bash, Write, Edit, MultiEdit, WebFetch, and WebSearch call is screened
before it runs — dangerous command patterns, outbound data leaks, and prompt
injection attempts get caught, not just logged. Web content fetched into a
session is scanned before it lands in context. This is on by default; there
is nothing to configure to get it.

**One rule that matters more than the rest: don't point this at client
source code or client data without checking first.** If you're not sure
whether something's in scope, ask before pasting it in.

## Memory

`MEMORY.md` in this directory is where anything worth remembering across
sessions goes — project conventions, things that didn't work, useful
context. Read it, edit it directly, or just ask Claude to remember
something and it'll add an entry. No special format required beyond a
short heading and a line or two.

## Reset

If a session or a change to this setup goes sideways, nothing here is
precious. Delete `MEMORY.md` and start a new one, or re-run the installer.
There's no state you can't walk back.

## Growing into more

This install intentionally skips PAI's fuller doctrine — the Algorithm
(structured multi-phase task execution), the ISA system (living
task/project specs), named skills, and a persistent assistant identity.
None of that is gone; it's just not loaded by default. If your work starts
wanting more structure, see `{{UPGRADE_DOC_PATH}}` for how to opt in
without starting over.
